---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const publicLaunch = process.env.PUBLIC_LAUNCH === '1';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial and evidence method — AgentSutra"
  description="How AgentSutra turns observations into accessible lessons without hiding uncertainty, provenance or corrections."
  canonicalPath="/method/"
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid shell">
      <p class="page-intro__context">Publication method</p>
      <div>
        <h1>How to trust a Field Note.</h1>
        <p class="page-intro__lead">
          Every lesson separates what happened, what it might mean, what it does not prove, and what
          changed after review.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>What every published note shows</h2>
      <ul class="trust-list">
        <li>One useful claim in plain language.</li>
        <li>What was observed, reproduced or measured.</li>
        <li>A visible limitation beside the advice.</li>
        <li>The method and sources available for inspection.</li>
        <li>Material corrections retained as part of the public record.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What the evidence labels mean</h2>
      <dl class="definition-list evidence-glossary">
        <dt>Observed</dt><dd>Seen in one stated setting; it may not generalise.</dd>
        <dt>Reproduced</dt><dd>Repeated under the stated conditions.</dd>
        <dt>Measured</dt><dd>Counted using the stated setup and denominator.</dd>
        <dt>Bounded</dt><dd>Useful only within the stated limits.</dd>
        <dt>Corrected</dt><dd>The published claim or evidence materially changed.</dd>
        <dt>Withdrawn</dt><dd>The claim is no longer supported.</dd>
      </dl>

      <h2>Corrections and AI use</h2>
      <p id="editor">
        Material corrections remain visible instead of silently replacing the earlier record.
        AgentSutra is an independent publication created and edited by <a
          href="https://github.com/pravindurgani"
          rel="author me">Pravin Durgani</a
        >. Instagram and TikTok can remain faceless and publication-led; the canonical site and
        professional portfolio identify the creator, so this is editorial distance rather than
        strict anonymity. AI may assist research, structure or production; Pravin remains
        accountable for the claim, evidence, limitation, sources and release decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        AgentSutra publishes sanitised mechanisms, never raw operational evidence, client
        identities, credentials, personal paths or infrastructure topology. An opaque private
        evidence identifier can preserve provenance without exposing its source.
      </p>

      <h2>How a note is made</h2>
      <ol class="step-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Observe:</strong> start from a real problem, experiment, failure or correction.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reduce:</strong> choose one central claim and the audience problem it resolves.
        </li>
        <li><strong>Prove:</strong> assemble an evidence pack appropriate to the claim’s risk.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Explain:</strong> build one Thread, a visible text equivalent and one practical transfer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review:</strong> run privacy, factual, accessibility, visual and production gates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Publish:</strong> release a canonical page, then adapt it without changing its central
          claim.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Learn:</strong> collect corrections, reader comprehension and interview explanations.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>For technical reviewers: internal review levels</h2>
      <p>
        These levels determine how much review a claim requires. They are not truth scores or reader
        difficulty ratings.
      </p>
      <dl class="definition-list">
        <dt>Class A · Explain</dt><dd>
          A mental model or personal observation. Requires honest framing, source notes where
          relevant and editorial review.
        </dd>
        <dt>Class B · Demonstrate</dt><dd>
          An implementation or incident. Requires a reproducible mechanism or clearly labelled
          historical evidence, plus limitations.
        </dd>
        <dt>Class C · Measure</dt><dd>
          A number, benchmark or comparison. Requires a versioned setup, denominator, environment,
          retained result and uncertainty.
        </dd>
        <dt>Class D · Protect</dt><dd>
          A security, safety, infrastructure or career claim. Requires the strongest review, current
          verification and explicit residual risk. Independent approval must come from a named human
          reviewer with relevant expertise, a disclosed relationship and a dated attestation; an AI
          critique cannot satisfy this requirement.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      {
        !publicLaunch && (
          <aside class="method-fixture-note">
            <strong>Engineering fixture · not a public lesson</strong>
            <p>
              FN-000 exists only in isolated test builds. It checks the publishing software and
              proves nothing about a real AI system, a useful lesson or audience comprehension.
            </p>
          </aside>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
